# tools/p/pond_enclosure_ephemeral_witness.rish -- what the enclosure forgets, proven rather than promised.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/p/pond_enclosure_ephemeral_witness.rish
#
# WHAT THIS HOLDS. Orbit three of the quest that retires ai-jail is "the memory that forgets" -- an
# enclosure whose $HOME and /tmp dissolve on exit while the pier persists, done when a planted secret
# written outside the pier is provably absent after the enclosure closes. Two guards already read the
# enclosure and neither asked that question: pond_policy_launcher_witness.rish reads what the launcher
# SPELLS, pond_enclosure_built_witness.rish reads what the plan BUILDS, and both are questions about
# what an agent can SEE. This one asks how long what it WRITES lasts.
#
# THE TWO LEGS. The plan leg classifies every mount row by lifetime -- a tmpfs dissolves, a read-only
# bind keeps nothing because nothing can be written, a read-write bind hands the byte to the host --
# and gates the record's own `ephemeral` claims against it. The metal leg plants one marker per
# candidate path inside a real enclosure, lets it close, and reads the host. Where the two disagree
# the scan refuses, because a classification nobody checked against a kernel is a claim.
#
# MEASURED ON THIS PIER `20260829`: the private home and /tmp came back FORGOTTEN, and /dev/shm,
# /tmp/.X11-unix and /run/user/<uid> came back CARRYING THE MARKER. Three writable host paths outlive
# the close, none of them under the pier, every one of them a jail default rather than a flag Pond
# passes. That is orbit three's own falsifier, met on metal, and the ceiling holds it at three.
#
# THE READING BESIDE IT. active-designing/20260829-054303_the-three-the-enclosure-keeps.md carries
# the argument this guard only counts: the lifetime table, the metal reading path by path, and what
# closing each of the three survivors would cost.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES NOT REACH. Whether a survivor SHOULD be closed. The runtime directory carries the
# Wayland socket and /dev/shm carries shared memory a browser needs, so closing one changes what a
# running agent can do -- a seat rather than a sweep, and the quest's own custody line names any
# round that weakens or reshapes an isolation boundary as check-in territory.
#
# ACCRETE-ONLY. This reads ai-jail's own plan and Pond's record and rewrites neither. The probe leg
# starts one enclosure and removes every marker it plants, on the host, whether it survived or not.
# The ENCLOSURE selector stays ai-jail until the switchover round lands behind its audit.

say "enclosure-ephemeral: Language EN -- an enclosure that forgets is a promise about time, so the reading is taken over time."
say "enclosure-ephemeral: Style Gauge, Meter -- each note names the path and where the host keeps it, so a count becomes a line to open."
say "enclosure-ephemeral: Lens TAME -- safety first: the plan roster and the probe roster are both bounded, the gate is proven from both sides, and the metal leg refuses to be skipped where it could have run."

let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/p/pond_enclosure_ephemeral_control.sh"]
assert control.ok else "enclosure-ephemeral: the control must complete -- ${control.out}"
say control.out
assert control.out contains "control_failures=0" else "enclosure-ephemeral: every planted behavior must hold"
assert control.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "enclosure-ephemeral: the control must report ok"
assert control.out contains "unforgotten_claim_refused=yes" else "enclosure-ephemeral: a kept path claimed ephemeral must refuse"
assert control.out contains "forgotten_claim_passes=yes" else "enclosure-ephemeral: an honest ephemeral claim must pass free"
assert control.out contains "ceiling_at_bound_passes=yes" else "enclosure-ephemeral: the ceiling must be proven from the passing side"
assert control.out contains "ceiling_one_past_refuses=yes" else "enclosure-ephemeral: the ceiling must be proven from the refusing side"
assert control.out contains "lift_absent_refuses=yes" else "enclosure-ephemeral: a missing plan reader must refuse rather than guess"

let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/p/pond_enclosure_ephemeral_scan.sh"]
assert scan.ok else "enclosure-ephemeral: the plan reading must complete -- ${scan.out}"
say scan.out
assert scan.out contains "unforgotten_claims=0" else "enclosure-ephemeral: no path the record calls ephemeral may be one the plan keeps"
assert scan.out contains "verdict=ok" else "enclosure-ephemeral: the plan reading must read ok"
assert scan.out contains "probe_read=no" else "enclosure-ephemeral: an ordinary run starts no enclosure"

let jail = run ["sh" "-c" "command -v ai-jail >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo JAIL_PRESENT || echo JAIL_ABSENT"]
assert jail.ok else "enclosure-ephemeral: the host reading must complete"
say jail.out
if (jail.out contains "JAIL_ABSENT") then say "enclosure-ephemeral: ai-jail is absent here, so the metal leg is skipped by the host rather than by the guard, and the plan reading above stands alone."
if (jail.out contains "JAIL_PRESENT") then say "enclosure-ephemeral: ai-jail stands here, so the reading below is the kernel's own answer and a skip refuses."

let probe = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/p/pond_enclosure_ephemeral_scan.sh" "--probe"]
assert probe.ok else "enclosure-ephemeral: the probe run must complete -- ${probe.out}"
say probe.out
assert probe.out contains "probe_disagreements=0" else "enclosure-ephemeral: the kernel and the plan must agree about what survives"
assert probe.out contains "verdict=ok" else "enclosure-ephemeral: the probe run must read ok"

say "GREEN: pond enclosure-ephemeral -- every path the record calls ephemeral dissolves, the survivors are counted and named, and where a jail stands the kernel has been asked."
